<header><p class="enc-kicker">Institution</p><h1 class="enc-title">University of Tehran</h1><p class="enc-meta"><span class="dates">1934</span> · <a href="/centuries/20th-century">20th century</a></p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">The University of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/tehran">Tehran</a> is the oldest modern university in <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/iran">Iran</a>, founded in 1934 under <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/reza-shah">Reza Shah</a> by bringing together earlier colleges of law, medicine, engineering and teacher training. It became the leading centre of Iranian higher education and a focus of political activism, from opposition to the shah to the student protests of 1999.</p></div>
